<title>NETHERLANDS: Ahold sees considerably higher 1997 result.</title>
<headline>Ahold sees considerably higher 1997 result.</headline>
<dateline>ZAANDAM, Netherlands 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch supermarkets group Ahold NV on Thursday repeated its forecast that 1997 net profit would be considerably higher than that of 1996.</p>
<p>In May, Ahold said it expected its 1997 full-year profit to increase by 30 to 45 percent from 1996, and earnings per share by 12 to 20 percent.</p>
<p>The company today reported net profit of 234.4 million guilders ($121 million) over the first quarter of 1997, a 69.4 percent year-on-year rise.</p>
